<PageTitle>On-demand loading — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="On-demand loading" Category="Data Grid" CategoryHref="demo/grid" ControlName="GridControl"
                   Tagline="Rows, groups, totals and exports fetched from a provider as they are needed, never all at once."
                   SourcePath="Grid/GridItemsProvider.cs;Grid/GridControl.ItemsProvider.cs;Grid/GridControl.ProviderGrouping.cs;Grid/GridControl.ProviderExport.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            An <code>ItemsProvider</code> replaces <code>DataSource</code> with a delegate the grid calls whenever it needs rows: the first
            window, a scroll past what is loaded, a new sort or search, an export. Each <code>GridItemsRequest</code> says what is wanted
            (<code>Purpose</code>), where in the result it starts (<code>StartIndex</code>, <code>Count</code>) and the current
            <code>Query</code>: sorts, filters, search text, group fields and the aggregates to compute. The provider translates that into its
            own LINQ or SQL and answers with a <code>GridItemsResult</code> of items and the total count. The grid keeps only a few recent
            ranges in memory.
        </p>
        <p>
            With <code>EnableProviderGrouping</code> the same delegate also serves the group tree. <code>Groups</code> asks for the top-level
            groups, <code>GroupChildren</code> for the groups under one of them and <code>GroupItems</code> for the rows under the innermost,
            each with the parent keys in <code>GroupRequest</code>. Groups start collapsed (<code>ProviderGroupsInitiallyCollapsed</code>), so
            opening one is what sends its request; <code>ProviderGroupPageSize</code> and <code>ProviderGroupItemPageSize</code> cap each page,
            and the grid adds a <em>Load more</em> row while the provider reports <code>HasMore</code>. Group counts and aggregates come from
            the provider too, so captions and footers are right before any row is loaded.
        </p>
        <p>
            <code>ExportProviderQueryAsync</code> exports the whole current query rather than the loaded window: it pages through
            <code>Export</code> requests of <code>ProviderExportPageSize</code> rows, reports each page through
            <code>ProviderExportProgressChanged</code>, and <code>CancelProviderExport</code> stops it. Column filters travel in the same request
            as <code>Query.Filters</code>; this example leaves column filtering off because its provider does not translate them.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="orders" Title="Twelve thousand orders, loaded group by group" RazorCode="@Code.Orders" CSharpCode="@Code.OrdersCs">
            <Description><p>The orders sit in an in-memory list behind a 90 ms delay (60 ms for export pages) and stand in for a database. Open a region to fetch its categories, open a category to fetch its first 75 rows, and use <em>Load more</em> for the rest; the line under the grid counts the requests and names the last one. Sorting a column or typing in the search box starts a new query. <em>Export all to CSV</em> writes every order that matches the search, 400 at a time, with progress and a Cancel.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="ExportCsvAsync" Disabled="@(_grid?.IsProviderExporting == true)">Export all to CSV</ButtonControl>
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="CancelExport" Disabled="@(_grid?.IsProviderExporting != true)">Cancel export</ButtonControl>
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <div class="orders">
                <GridControl @ref="_grid"
                             TValue="ProviderOrder"
                             ItemsProvider="LoadOrdersAsync"
                             ItemKeySelector="@(row => row.Id)"
                             Height="520px"
                             AllowGrouping="true"
                             GroupColumns="@_groups"
                             EnableProviderGrouping="true"
                             ProviderGroupsInitiallyCollapsed="true"
                             ProviderGroupPageSize="2"
                             ProviderGroupItemPageSize="75"
                             ShowGroupCount="true"
                             AllowSorting="true"
                             ShowSearchBar="true"
                             AllowResizing="true"
                             ProviderExportPageSize="400"
                             ProviderExportProgressChanged="OnExportProgress"
                             ShowRowCountInFooter="true"
                             AggregateRows="@_aggregates">
                    <GridColumnsBase>
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ProviderOrder.Id)" HeaderText="Order" Width="90px" Type="ColumnType.Number" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ProviderOrder.Region)" HeaderText="Region" Width="120px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ProviderOrder.Category)" HeaderText="Category" Width="140px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ProviderOrder.Customer)" HeaderText="Customer" Width="220px" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ProviderOrder.OrderDate)" HeaderText="Date" Width="110px" Type="ColumnType.Date" Format="d" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ProviderOrder.Quantity)" HeaderText="Qty" Width="80px" Type="ColumnType.Number" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" />
                        <GridColumn Field="@nameof(ProviderOrder.Amount)" HeaderText="Amount" Width="120px" Type="ColumnType.Number" Format="C2" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" />
                    </GridColumnsBase>
                </GridControl>
                </div>
                <p class="result">@_lastRequest @ExportText</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
        <DemoExample Id="search" Title="A flat list, searched, sorted and paged by the provider" RazorCode="@Code.Search" CSharpCode="@Code.SearchCs">
            <Description><p>The rate card is an in-memory list of 5,000 lines synthesized for each visitor and stands in for a database: each line is one supplier's service at one destination, with the net rate the operator pays. The provider gets every request the grid makes and returns only the range asked for, with the total. Type in the search box and the next request carries <code>SearchText</code>, which this provider matches against the code, description and supplier; sort a column and it carries <code>Sorts</code>; scroll and the grid asks for the next range. The line under the grid describes the last request. Column filters are off because this provider does not translate them.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <GridControl TValue="RateCardItem"
                             ItemsProvider="LoadItemsAsync"
                             Height="380px"
                             AllowSorting="true"
                             AllowFiltering="false"
                             AllowSelection="true"
